🚀 The feature, motivation and pitch
In current code, when we used class RegisterDispatchKey to generate code, the following template is fixed and cannot add additional logic to the code.



      pytorch/torchgen/dest/register_dispatch_key.py


        Lines 537 to 549
      in
      f79d2b4







                           return f"""\ 




           namespace {{ 









           {returns_type} {name}({args_str}) {{ 




             {device_check} 









             {device_guard} 




             return {impl_name}({args_exprs_str}); 




           }} 









           }} // anonymous namespace 




           """ 










The reason we want to add custom code is because we have some of our own tools, like precision comparison tools. Before each operator is called, our tools's API needs to be called. And if this part of the code is added in each operator implementation, the code is too redundant and easy to forget . So we want RegisterDispatchKey to be extended for custom code like #101333
Alternatives
I think by passing in a custom template or a {custom code} reserving placeholders +callback functions.
If there is a better way to implement it, please tell me what I should do.
