🚀 The feature, motivation and pitch
I am studying non-blocking sendrecv, which means that a series of send and recv operations need to be put into a group. For the NCCL backend, there are explicit interfaces to call _group_start() and _group_end(). However, for third-party communication backends, this means that PyTorch needs to be modified. Is it possible to add an interface _group_start() and _group_end() in ProcessGroup or Backend, so that third-party communication libraries can easily implement non-blocking send and recv?
torch/distributed/distributed_c10d.py:
@contextlib.contextmanager
def _batch_p2p_manager(backend):
    if backend == Backend.NCCL:
        ProcessGroupNCCL._group_start()
    try:
        yield
    finally:
        if backend == Backend.NCCL:
            ProcessGroupNCCL._group_end()

